Z||000000||soup||12-12-2001||04:46 AM||||My speedo light is out, has been since i got the car last month, its an 87 GT with T-Tops. Can anyone tell me how to access the light, I took off the back of the gauge console and I couldnt find a light that was for the speedo (There were only 3 bulbs actually in there, luckily i had extra plugs, and bulbs) DO i actually need to take out the speedo?<P>Thanks for the help in advance, i love this forum, you guys are very helpfull, I hope to have my pics up soon as well.||||reg||5
Z||000001||GTDude||12-12-2001||05:13 AM||||No, if you can see the bulb sockets, this is all there is, if they aren't burning, try bulbs, or try bending the little brass tabs so they make better contact.  If this doesn't work......and the other lights do...then you have a burned out printed circuit board.<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||12-12-2001||10:30 AM||||First of all, if you only have three lights in the back of the guage panel you are missing quite a few ....... there should be 17 lights there!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg">  <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
